new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ed23b94
--- /dev/null
+++ b/README-linux.md
@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# FidelityFX SDK 1.1.4: native Linux port of the Vulkan `ffx_api` library (milestone 1)
+
+> **Unofficial build.** This is an unofficial build of AMD FidelityFX SDK 1.1.4, modified to build on Linux. It is not
+> made, endorsed or supported by AMD. AMD's copyright and MIT licence (`LICENSE.txt`) apply to AMD's code; our changes
+> are under the same MIT licence. FidelityFX and FSR are AMD trademarks, used here only to name the software.
+
+Base: `GPUOpen-LibrariesAndSDKs/FidelityFX-SDK` tag `v1.1.4`, commit `c6efa6bf7f2027b3ec94f28578bb5965eabb9e55`
+(MIT licence, see `LICENSE.txt`). Branch `linux-port`; every change is either `#ifdef _WIN32`-guarded or
+harmless on Windows, so the commits can be exported as a patch series onto the pinned upstream commit.
+
+Result: `libamd_fidelityfx_vk.so`, a drop-in for `amd_fidelityfx_vk.dll`. It exports exactly
+`ffxCreateContext`, `ffxDestroyContext`, `ffxConfigure`, `ffxQuery`, `ffxDispatch` and has the providers
+FSR3 upscaler, frame generation (frame interpolation + optical flow) and the Vulkan frame-generation
+swapchain. FSR2 is left out (`FFX_DISABLE_FSR2`). It links the system `libvulkan.so.1`, libc and libm;
+libstdc++/libgcc are linked statically.
+
+## Build
+
+    linux/build.sh            # configure, generate shaders, build, into ./build-linux
+    build-linux/ffx_smoke build-linux/libamd_fidelityfx_vk.so
+
+Needs cmake, ninja, gcc or clang, `glslangValidator` (tested with 16.6.0) and the Vulkan headers/loader.
+Heavy compiles: run under `systemd-run --user --scope -p MemoryMax=6G ...` (about 1.5 GB peak here).
+
+## What was changed
+
+- **Shaders.** The repo has no prebuilt SPIR-V. AMD's shader compiler front end `FidelityFX_SC` is built on
+  Linux from the repo's own source (`sdk/tools/ffx_shader_compiler`, GLSL path only, HLSL/DXC/FXC `#ifdef _WIN32`),
+  and `linux/CMakeLists.txt` drives it with AMD's own `CMakeShaders*.txt` lists, so the permutation matrix is
+  AMD's. `linux/shaders` is a symlink to `sdk/src/backends/vk/shaders` (their globs are relative).
+  `CMakeCompileShaders.txt`: on UNIX the `-DOPT={0,1}` arguments are single-quoted, because `/bin/sh` may be bash
+  and would brace-expand them. `glsl_compiler.cpp` only strips a trailing `\r` from glslang messages.
+- **Win32 compat layer** `linux/compat/ffx_linux_compat.h` (force-included with `-include`; `Windows.h` etc. in
+  that folder resolve to it): `CRITICAL_SECTION` = `std::recursive_mutex`, auto-reset events =
+  mutex + condition variable, `CreateThread`/`WaitForSingleObject` = `std::thread`,
+  `QueryPerformanceCounter` = `steady_clock` ns with frequency 1e9, `SetThreadDescription` = `pthread_setname_np`,
+  `SetThreadPriority` = no-op, `wcscpy_s`/`sprintf_s`/`swprintf_s`/`_countof`. This keeps the swapchain diff tiny.
+- **Source edits:** `FFX_API_ENTRY` (visibility attribute), `ffx_provider.cpp` (no D3D12/external providers
+  on Linux, FSR2 optional), `ui64` literals -> `ULL`, `%s` -> `%ls` for wide strings, full-screen-exclusive
+  structs under `_WIN32`, `static_cast` of `void*` to function pointer -> `reinterpret_cast`, two rvalue-to-reference
+  calls, `FFX_UNUSED` include, `FFX_SDK_DEFAULT_CONTEXT_SIZE` doubled on Linux (`wchar_t` is 4 bytes, the private
+  contexts outgrew the public blob), and `ffx_vk.cpp` scratch-memory arrays aligned to 16 bytes (gcc emits `movaps`
+  for them; the 4-byte alignment faulted only in optimised builds).
+- Export control: `linux/ffx_api.map` (version script) + `-fvisibility=hidden`.
+
+## Measured
+
+- 28 shader files x 4 variants (wave32/wave64, fp32/fp16) = 112 header sets, 2968 permutations requested,
+  252 unique SPIR-V blobs; 0 failures; all 252 pass `spirv-val --target-env vulkan1.2`.
+- `nm -D` shows only the five exports. gcc 16 warnings: 4 (deprecated `wstring_convert`, one `-Wwrite-strings`).
+- `ffx_smoke` (headless, RTX 3070): FSR3 upscaler create/query/destroy and frame generation create/destroy all return OK.
+
+## Not tested / known gaps
+
+- The swapchain provider (`FGSWAPCHAIN_VK`): compiled and linked only; never created, presented or paced.
+  Presenter threads run at normal priority (no RT rights); the pacer busy-waits on a CPU core, as on Windows.
+- No dispatch (`ffxDispatch`) of any effect, so no shader has run on a GPU; no Vulkan validation layer was installed here.
+- FSR2 provider omitted; HLSL path of SC not ported; clang build not tried; `wstring_convert` (deprecated) is AMD's own Linux fallback.
+- The app must enable `VK_KHR_get_memory_requirements2` and `VK_KHR_dedicated_allocation` on its device when the driver
+  offers them: the backend loads the KHR-named entry points by name and calls them without a null check (same on Windows).
+- Not AMD's binary: ship `LICENSE.txt` with it, and name it as your own build.
